      "message": "The problem we\u0027re having in the Trusty driver is that we\u0027re passing in the value of the guests\u0027s `smp_processor_id()` here, which is the vcpu id which doesn\u0027t match the physical cpu number (0 vs 2 in our case). Is there a way for a guest to get the current physical processor, or should we map it here?\n\nWe should probably stop using `smp_processor_id`, but then we still have the problem of \"which endpoint id does Trusty pass to FFA_RUN?\"",
